WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.592 --> 00:00:17.722
June 4 Dear Daddy Longlegs, We're very busy right now.

2
00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:20.044
Exams start tomorrow.

3
00:00:21.705 --> 00:00:24.827
The weather is so lovely, but there's no time to enjoy it.

4
00:00:26.128 --> 00:00:26.528
Oh well.

5
00:00:26.948 --> 00:00:27.849
Vacation's coming.

6
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.312
We took a break from studying today to discuss our summer plans.

7
00:00:34.588 --> 00:00:37.130
"I'm going to Europe again," Julia said.

8
00:00:39.131 --> 00:00:40.091
I put down my pen.

9
00:00:40.111 --> 00:00:42.593
"Oh, you're so lucky!"

10
00:00:42.613 --> 00:00:45.494
"I guess so.

11
00:00:45.994 --> 00:00:49.777
But sometimes I get bored being away from my friends for the whole summer.

12
00:00:50.777 --> 00:00:52.318
This will be my fourth trip."

13
00:00:54.039 --> 00:00:56.940
I'd be happy to go on my first trip—or my tenth!

14
00:00:58.281 --> 00:01:00.302
But I didn't want to act like I was jealous.

15
00:01:02.083 --> 00:01:02.904
Even though I was!

16
00:01:04.596 --> 00:01:06.538
"I'm going to our summer house in the mountains."

17
00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:07.759
Sallie looked at me.

18
00:01:07.779 --> 00:01:10.461
"I wish you were coming with me."

19
00:01:10.481 --> 00:01:12.303
"So do I.

20
00:01:12.783 --> 00:01:15.065
But my guardian would never agree to that.

21
00:01:16.306 --> 00:01:18.028
I didn't even dare to ask."

22
00:01:19.849 --> 00:01:20.730
Julia looked at me.

23
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:24.513
"Are you going back to that farm in the middle of nowhere?"

24
00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:27.716
"Yes, at the end of the summer.

25
00:01:28.957 --> 00:01:30.578
But first I'm tutoring Mrs.

26
00:01:30.698 --> 00:01:32.180
Charles Paterson's daughters.

27
00:01:33.696 --> 00:01:35.617
We'll be staying at their cottage at the beach."

28
00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:41.280
"Mrs. Paterson is a friend of my mother's," Sallie explained to Julia.

29
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:46.042
"She met Judy at our house during Christmas vacation sophomore year.

30
00:01:47.863 --> 00:01:50.504
You must have made a good impression," she said to me.

31
00:01:50.524 --> 00:01:53.905
"Mrs. Paterson seems nice," I said.

32
00:01:53.925 --> 00:01:55.926
"And she's generous.

33
00:01:57.327 --> 00:01:59.308
She's paying me fifty dollars a month.

34
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.163
I'd be happy with twenty-five, but I wasn't going to say no to fifty!"

35
00:02:05.864 --> 00:02:06.905
Julia shook her head.

36
00:02:06.925 --> 00:02:10.407
"I'm glad I don't have to worry about money.

37
00:02:10.427 --> 00:02:12.188
It's so boring."

38
00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:17.332
As soon as Julia left the room, Sallie rolled her eyes.

39
00:02:17.352 --> 00:02:21.715
"It must be nice to be able to buy whatever you want."

40
00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:23.496
I shrugged.

41
00:02:23.516 --> 00:02:28.680
"Maybe money is boring, but I'm looking forward to earning some this summer.

42
00:02:29.932 --> 00:02:33.414
I'm also eager to see the Semples and my favorite farm animals."

43
00:02:35.795 --> 00:02:37.957
I must tell you one more thing, Daddy Longlegs.

44
00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:43.680
Sallie's brother, Jimmy, and his roommate, Bill, are graduating from Princeton this week.

45
00:02:45.101 --> 00:02:47.502
Sallie and I really wanted to go to the ceremony.

46
00:02:49.563 --> 00:02:51.044
But we have exams that day.

47
00:02:52.545 --> 00:02:53.846
A bitter disappointment!

48
00:02:55.347 --> 00:02:57.448
I must stop writing and do some more studying.

49
00:02:58.996 --> 00:03:08.519
Yours, Judy June 10 Dear Daddy Longlegs, This is the hardest letter I've ever written.

50
00:03:09.439 --> 00:03:12.760
But I've decided what I must do, so there's no turning back.

51
00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:17.822
It's very generous of you to offer to send me to Europe this summer.

52
00:03:19.062 --> 00:03:20.843
I was very tempted to say yes!

53
00:03:22.363 --> 00:03:23.924
But then I took some time to think.

54
00:03:26.644 --> 00:03:30.966
I can't refuse to take your money for college, and then accept it for travel.

55
00:03:31.947 --> 00:03:35.069
Besides, I don't want to get used to too many luxuries.

56
00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.631
A trip to Europe is definitely a luxury!

57
00:03:40.672 --> 00:03:43.313
I want to go, but I don't need to go.

58
00:03:45.194 --> 00:03:47.635
Sometimes it's hard to live with Julia and Sallie.

59
00:03:50.277 --> 00:03:52.718
They think the world owes them everything they want.

60
00:03:54.179 --> 00:03:55.980
But I know that's not true for me.

61
00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.741
Thank you again for your nice offer.

62
00:04:00.842 --> 00:04:02.824
Don't be angry with me for refusing.

63
00:04:04.285 --> 00:04:05.886
I appreciate your kindness.

64
00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.086
I really do.

65
00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.789
But you've already done so much for me.

66
00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:20.596
Yours, Judy June 14 Dear Daddy Longlegs, I'm at the beach with Mrs.

67
00:04:20.656 --> 00:04:22.217
Paterson and her two daughters.

68
00:04:23.858 --> 00:04:26.420
I left college a few days earlier than I'd planned.

69
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:28.508
Here's what happened.

70
00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:32.930
I was in the middle of exams when Jervie showed up again.

71
00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.011
He took me to tea in town.

72
00:04:40.772 --> 00:04:42.712
going to Europe this summer," he announced.

73
00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:44.673
I laughed.

74
00:04:44.693 --> 00:04:47.974
"It sounds like all the Pendletons will be there.

75
00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.495
Are you going with Julia and her family?"

76
00:04:51.515 --> 00:04:54.376
"No, I'm going by myself."

77
00:04:56.148 --> 00:05:00.289
"My guardian offered to send me to Europe with a lady who's chaperoning a group of girls."

78
00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:04.730
I stirred some sugar into my tea.

79
00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.771
"But I decided not to go."

80
00:05:07.791 --> 00:05:11.672
"Oh, you shouldn't say no to an opportunity like that!

81
00:05:13.073 --> 00:05:15.433
Seeing Europe is an important part of your education."

82
00:05:16.854 --> 00:05:17.674
He grinned at me.

83
00:05:17.694 --> 00:05:21.395
"I could arrange to be in Paris when you're there.

84
00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:25.656
We could run away from the chaperone and have dinner at a nice French restaurant."

85
00:05:27.612 --> 00:05:28.153
I laughed.

86
00:05:28.593 --> 00:05:31.995
"That's very tempting, but I can't go."

87
00:05:33.916 --> 00:05:37.138
When I tried to explain why I couldn't go, he wouldn't listen.

88
00:05:37.158 --> 00:05:40.160
"You're a silly, stubborn child!"

89
00:05:40.421 --> 00:05:41.021
Jervie said.

90
00:05:42.222 --> 00:05:43.663
"You don't know what's good for you."

91
00:05:45.124 --> 00:05:46.705
He kept insisting I go.

92
00:05:48.186 --> 00:05:49.967
That made me so angry!

93
00:05:49.987 --> 00:05:52.989
I don't like feeling forced to do something.

94
00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.152
I was glad to finish our tea and get back to studying.

95
00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:03.743
As soon as exams were over, I packed my bags and left for Mrs.

96
00:06:03.783 --> 00:06:07.986
Paterson's. And now I'm here by the sea.

97
00:06:09.507 --> 00:06:12.509
Yours, Judy P.S.

98
00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:14.291
I told Jervie about you.

99
00:06:16.753 --> 00:06:19.375
He thinks you're my guardian and an old family friend.

100
00:06:21.196 --> 00:06:24.719
He knows I'm an orphan, but I didn't dare mention the John Grier Home.
